Pre-requisite:
- Python3.10 is mandatory

About:
- Running TF-M on rpi_pico2(rp2350) along with non-secure application example.

Steps:
- make --> this takes care of setting up required repo(trusted-firmware-m,pico-sdk,openocd) and venv.
- make flash --> uses openocd


Commands used for building binaries spe and nspe binaries for rp2350:
------ SPE --------
cmake -S /Users/bharathkammara/Desktop/rpi_pico2/tfm_s_ns/trusted-firmware-m \
-B build/spe \
-DTFM_PLATFORM=rpi/rp2350 \
-DTFM_PROFILE=profile_medium \
-DMCUBOOT_IMAGE_NUMBER=1 \
-DTFM_BL2_LOG_LEVEL=LOG_LEVEL_VERBOSE \
-DLOG_LEVEL=LOG_LEVEL_DEBUG \
-DPython3_EXECUTABLE=/Users/bharathkammara/Desktop/rpi_pico2/cortex_m33_tf-m/venv/bin/python3 \
cmake --build build/spe -- install

------ NSPE --------
cmake -S /Users/bharathkammara/Desktop/rpi_pico2/tfm_s_ns/tf-m-extras/examples/tf-m-example-ns-app \
-B build/nspe \
-DCONFIG_SPE_PATH=/Users/bharathkammara/Desktop/rpi_pico2/tfm_s_ns/build/spe/api_ns \
-DPython3_EXECUTABLE=/Users/bharathkammara/Desktop/rpi_pico2/cortex_m33_tf-m/venv/bin/python3 \
-DFETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_PICO_SDK=/Users/bharathkammara/Desktop/rpi_pico2/tfm_s_ns/pico-sdk \
cmake --build build/nspe